STGR PATCH: 0006 — STGR update system (GitHub Releases based)
Purpose:                Implement the in-browser STGR update check. Queries the configured
                        STGR GitHub Releases repository, validates product / version /
                        architecture / SHA256 (signature when available), and never
                        auto-executes downloads. The updater is user-triggered only
                        (no idle network activity) via the About UI / preferences.
Files changed:          browser/components/stgr/updater/STGRUpdater.sys.mjs (new)
                        browser/components/stgr/updater/moz.build (new)
Security impact:        Update packages are validated (HTTPS, product, version, arch, hash)
                        before any download or launch. Downgrades and unknown releases are
                        rejected. No silent execution of downloaded files.
Performance impact:     None when idle — the module performs no background activity.
Upstream compatibility: Uses stable ESM + fetch APIs; rebase risk LOW.
Note:                   Full preferences-pane wiring is Phase 9 of the roadmap; v1 exposes
                        the same validation logic via scripts/check_update.py (CI + CLI).

